@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# Release archive hygiene
+
+Never distribute a ZIP made by zipping the checkout directory. It can include populated `.env` files, `.git`, dependencies, test caches, bytecode, and build output.
+
+## Preferred release from a reviewed commit
+
+`git archive` includes only tracked files from the selected commit. It is safe only after the secret/generated-file check passes and credentials have been rotated; it cannot remove secrets from Git history by itself.
+
+```bash
+mkdir -p build/releases
+python scripts/secure_repository_hygiene.py --strict
+git archive --format=zip --prefix=PatentShield/ -o build/releases/PatentShield.zip HEAD
+python scripts/verify_release_archive.py build/releases/PatentShield.zip
+```
+
+## Sanitized export of a worktree
+
+To include reviewed local modifications before committing them, use the allowlisted exporter. It enumerates tracked and non-ignored untracked files but filters secret environment files, VCS directories, caches, dependency trees, generated output, bytecode, private keys, and local database artifacts. The verifier then independently inspects the actual ZIP.
+
+```bash
+python scripts/create_release_archive.py build/releases/PatentShield-release-candidate.zip
+python scripts/verify_release_archive.py build/releases/PatentShield-release-candidate.zip
+```
+
+The release gate performs these steps automatically and also runs `secure_repository_hygiene.py --strict`. If the repository index still tracks `.env` or generated output, that check intentionally blocks the release until the paths are untracked. For example:
+
+```bash
+git rm --cached -- .env backend/.env frontend/.env
+# inspect and untrack any further findings printed by secure_repository_hygiene.py
+python scripts/secure_repository_hygiene.py --strict
+```
+
+Keep local secret files on disk only when needed, but do not commit them. Rotate any real credentials that have ever entered a ZIP or Git history. Use a reviewed history-rewrite procedure if policy requires removing historical secret blobs; a new clean archive does not erase old Git objects or prior distributions.

